Track B (mode 'g') enabler.  Ports the minimum subset of
EP4CE6/fuzz/bitstream.py needed for on-chip "(x, y, n, 16-bit mask)
→ flip CRAM cells + repair frame CRC" — restricted to pin-friendly
columns X∈{10,16,22,28} so the 35-cell canon transition layer is a
no-op and the C codec doesn't need to carry it.

New files:
  host/gen_lutcodec_data.py
    Build-time generator.  Calls _sigma_inv_lookup(foff, fb8, group)
    for each pin-friendly (x, y, n) triple and emits
    sw/stage2_loader/lutcodec_data.h with a 1152-byte packed σ⁻¹
    table (2 bits per σ⁻¹ component × 4 = 1 byte/position) + the
    parallel COLUMN_BASE / LAB_Y / SLOT_BASE tables the C port reads.
    Sourced from $EP4CE6_REPO (default /home/test/EP4CE6).
    Output is gitignored — regenerated every build, like rot_golden.h.

  sw/stage2_loader/lutcodec.{c,h}
    On-chip address-formula port of LutCodec.from_cram_model +
    predict_sram + write_tt.  lc_init(x,y,n) does table lookup +
    slot-1 wrap math; lut_apply_mask(rbf, lc, mask, dirty) XOR-flips
    the cells for each set mask bit and (optionally) marks touched
    CRAM frames in a caller-supplied bitmap for CRC repair.
    Compact LE descriptor (12 B) — no per-position cell arrays in
    .rodata; cells are computed on demand from σ⁻¹ + sigma_inv table.

  sw/stage2_loader/crc16.{c,h}
    CRC-16/IBM reflected (poly 0xA001, init 0xFE54) for CRAM frames
    25..1751 — direct port of crc16_rbf_frame + patch_rbf_crc.
    Adds lc_patch_rbf_crc_frames (dirty-bitmap variant) and
    lc_mark_dirty (called from lut_apply_mask).

  host/test_lutcodec_c.py
    ctypes cross-validation gate.  Compiles lutcodec.c + crc16.c as a
    host shared library and asserts byte-identical RBF output vs the
    Python LutCodec.write_tt + patch_rbf_crc reference for 100
    random tuples over the pin-friendly subset.  Run:
      EP4CE6_REPO=/home/test/EP4CE6 python3 host/test_lutcodec_c.py
    Currently passes 200/200 byte-identical at seed=20260516 + 42.

Edits:
  rtl/ax301_top.vhd
    IMEM_SIZE 16*1024 → 32*1024.  Phase 7 σ⁻¹ table + crc/lutcodec
    code overshoot the 16 KB budget (plan v2 §Phase 7 — ~30 KB tables
    + 3 KB code anticipated; actual ~3 KB σ⁻¹ table + 2 KB code, well
    inside 32 KB).  Adds one M9K row per NEORV32 IMEM doc; still
    within the 10,320-LE jailbreak budget.

  sw/stage2_loader/Makefile
    __neorv32_rom_size 16k → 32k (linker side of the IMEM bump).
    New lutcodec_data phony target + lutcodec.c prereq mirror the
    existing rot_golden pattern.

  .gitignore
    Added sw/stage2_loader/lutcodec_data.h.

Dead-stripped pending Phase 8: lutcodec / crc16 symbols compile cleanly
into the build dir but are not yet referenced by main.c (mode 'g'
handler is Phase 8).  Stage2 binary therefore stays at 9492 B.
